1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,204
This spoon

2
00:00:01,304 --> 00:00:03,830
weighs a billion tons.

3
00:00:03,930 --> 00:00:04,810
No, seriously.

4
00:00:04,910 --> 00:00:07,035
It's one teaspoon of neutron star.

5
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:10,065
It starts as a giant star

6
00:00:11,150 --> 00:00:12,105
Supernova!

7
00:00:12,205 --> 00:00:13,275
The core collapses

8
00:00:13,450 --> 00:00:15,142
into a neutron star.

9
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:17,697
Atoms are mostly empty space.

10
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:18,998
Gravity crushes them

11
00:00:19,098 --> 00:00:20,935
into neutrons, packed tight.

12
00:00:20,970 --> 00:00:21,899
One teaspoon

13
00:00:21,999 --> 00:00:23,437
about a billion tons,

14
00:00:23,537 --> 00:00:24,931
as much as a small mountain.

15
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:26,518
Wait, it gets weirder.

16
00:00:26,618 --> 00:00:27,236
It spins.

17
00:00:27,336 --> 00:00:28,565
It's a pulsar.

18
00:00:28,665 --> 00:00:30,793
Some spin hundreds of times a second.

19
00:00:30,893 --> 00:00:32,506
Two beams sweep through space,

20
00:00:32,606 --> 00:00:33,811
so don't stand in the way.

21
00:00:33,911 --> 00:00:35,270
A cosmic lighthouse.

22
00:00:35,450 --> 00:00:37,675
So next time you look up at the pretty stars,

23
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:38,505
remember,

24
00:00:38,605 --> 00:00:40,240
one of them is so dense,

25
00:00:40,950 --> 00:00:42,015
a teaspoon of it

26
00:00:42,115 --> 00:00:43,500
weighs like a mountain.

27
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:51,475
Space is ridiculous.

